Alter _what_? Alter the potions using an altar? 

Anyway, there are some principles you may find useful:

1) In nethack, in general, if you have a choice between taking a risk
   now or deferring it until later, pick "later" -- you will be better-
   prepared to deal with it should things go wrong.

   It's no use turning potions to water until you have a use for potions
   of water. If you've found no altar yet, why not put it off until later?

   For potions specifically, I usually do little with un-IDed ones in
   the early game other than keep them safe until I have a unihorn and
   darts, and can #dip-ID the bad ones (or immediately fix bad effects
   -- other than sleep -- induced by those that don't coat or poly
   darts, and which aren't cleared by the horn).

2) Playing with fountains is dangerous in a number of ways. Dipping
   !?+ to clear them has a bad risk/reward ratio, and the risks include
   having the fountain dry up.

   Better, IMHO, to pick one centrally-located fountain, stand on it,
   dig down with a pick-axe to make pools. Then you can drop everything
   you don't want wet on land, and jump in until your !?+ are clear.

   Worst risks are drowning your pet, and having monsters show up while
   you don't have your full gear. Still much nicer than demons and nymphs,
   and never runs out.

   Dipping cursed items in fountains to get them uncursed can be handy
   in an extreme emergency, or if you're buff enough to take the worst
   possible outcome in stride.


